&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The AI Teams at Agile Robots&lt;/strong&gt; are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Robotics Software Engineer (m/f/d) AI Tools &amp;amp; Integration&lt;/strong&gt;, who will integrate AI models with robot hardware and build the applications and tooling around them. Customers and partners reuse this stack through open-source releases, so it has to keep working with messy data, limited compute, and real hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Robot Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Integrate trained AI models with single-arm and dual-arm robots through ROS 2, and maintain the runtime that runs them on hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Build robot applications on top of the AI stack, including agentic workflows that chain AI models and robot skills into multi-step tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tool Interfaces:&lt;/strong&gt; Build UI, API, and CLI tools such as dataset viewers, training dashboards, and benchmark viewers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Testing:&lt;/strong&gt; Build test suites that run real user workflows from data through training to inference, including stress tests with messy data and limited compute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Readiness:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain nightly regression runs on the reference workflows and run reliability checks before demos and open-source releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Write and maintain the documentation customers and partners use to adopt the tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Degree in Computer Science, Robotics, or a related field, or equivalent qualification plus professional experience building comparable software systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Python Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Professional experience building and maintaining Python software that other engineers depend on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROS 2 Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience integrating and debugging software on physical robots through ROS 2.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Containers &amp;amp; CI:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with Docker and CI pipelines such as GitHub Actions for reproducible builds and releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience designing integration and end-to-end test suites and debugging failures across the full stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Services:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience building backend services and APIs, for example with FastAPI or gRPC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C++ Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience writing C++ for robot-side or performance-critical code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agentic Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience building applications that combine language or vision-language models with robot skill execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Working experience with React or Next.js for building data-heavy interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ML Workflows:&lt;/strong&gt; Working understanding of how training and inference pipelines for robot learning models fit together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;TranslationField-module__fieldItemName___Q0F_7 TranslationField-module__aboutUsWrapper___WXJpq&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
