&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us in our mission to transform the way people shop and eat, where impact, innovation and growth drive everything we do. Our Engineering teams tackle complex technical challenges across a global, three-sided marketplace, building and scaling systems that serve millions of customers, riders and partners every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From real-time logistics to resilient infrastructure and marketplace optimisation, we design, build and operate technology that powers Deliveroo’s growth at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In November 2023 we launched our non-food retail offering, Deliveroo ‘Shopping’, where we work with large and small merchants. We oversee all operations within the grocery and retail ecosystem, ensuring stores are equipped to receive and efficiently process orders. Our solutions empower stores to manage orders seamlessly through multiple channels, including our in-house app, API integration, and devices pre-installed with our software. Additionally, we provide tools to maintain and update product catalogs, ensuring accurate inventory for consumers. The technology we’ve developed enables our partners to pick the correct items swiftly while keeping inventory data current, optimizing both efficiency and accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Staff Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;London, UK - Hybrid (3 days from the office)&lt;/strong&gt; team. In this role, you’ll help us define technical solutions for critical business problems and lead the technical direction for complex, high-scale systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get to know our&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.deliveroo.co.uk/software-engineering-at-deliveroo/&quot;&gt; Engineering&lt;/a&gt; team — what drives us, how we work, and what you can expect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be joining a high-impact engineering group focused on solving unstructured and ambiguous challenges. You will act as a technical authority, aligning non-adjacent teams to deliver results that move the needle for the entire organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here’s what your day-to-day might look like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Technical Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a subject matter expert, providing high-level reviews and technical advice across multiple teams.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect Scalable Solutions:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and design technical solutions for complex business problems within a high-traffic environment (20krpm+).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Strategic Direction:&lt;/strong&gt; Influence the long-term technical roadmap and manage project timelines, risks, and sustainable delivery paces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor &amp;amp; Coach:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the growth of engineers across all levels and partner with up-and-coming leaders to scale our engineering culture.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead engineering interviews and contribute to recruiting strategy to ensure we maintain a high bar for talent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need to Thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ideal candidate will bring strong expertise in some of these areas and curiosity to grow in others:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep Technical Mastery:&lt;/strong&gt; Significant experience building web-based applications at scale and a pride in writing readable, well-tested software.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Polyglot Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in (or a strong desire to learn) languages such as &lt;strong&gt;(Go, Ruby/Rails, Python, Scala, React or Rust)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed Systems Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience with relational databases &lt;strong&gt;(PostgreSQL) and NoSQL backends (Redis, DynamoDB, or Elasticsearch).&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-Scale Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to design and operate systems handling massive request volumes and complex logistical workflows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong understanding of how to align multiple disciplines and teams to resolve ambiguous technical challenges.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Deliveroo, you’ll do work that matters—solving real-world problems in a three-sided marketplace that’s constantly evolving. We’re food lovers, problem solvers, community organisers, proud parents, and more, brought together by a shared drive to make things better. Working here you can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;🔧 &lt;strong&gt;Solve meaningful problems at real scale&lt;/strong&gt; Work on a complex, always-on marketplace that impacts millions every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;🌱 &lt;strong&gt;See your impact, fast&lt;/strong&gt; Ship, test and improve ideas quickly in a low-hierarchy, high-ownership environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;🧠 &lt;strong&gt;Grow through challenge and ownership&lt;/strong&gt; Take on big, ambiguous problems and accelerate your career with strong support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;🌎 &lt;strong&gt;A culture built for builders&lt;/strong&gt; High standards, collaboration, flexible working and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;​​💰 &lt;strong&gt;Share in the success you help create&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive salary and equity options, so you’re rewarded for the impact you make.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DASH Brands will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about DASH Brands&#39; legitimate recruiting process at&lt;/em&gt; &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _2rkolb4i _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-is-router-link=&quot;false&quot; data-testid=&quot;link-with-safety&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Associate Director, Medical Advisor, EU West, you will report to the Medical Director EU West and provide scientific leadership for three rare-disease launch programs in achondroplasia, limb-girdle muscular dystrophy, and genetic hypocalcaemia. You will translate global strategy into a focused country medical plan, build trusted partnerships across the French rare-disease ecosystem, and ensure high-quality, compliant execution in an agile affiliate environment. The main focus will be France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Medical strategy and execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Co-develop and execute the France Medical Affairs plan for the three portfolio programs, with clear priorities, milestones, KPIs, resource needs, and budget assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scientific leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain deep expertise in the diseases, patient journeys, standards of care, competitive environment, and emerging evidence; translate complex data into accurate and relevant scientific narratives for French stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and sustain peer-to-peer relationships with key experts, multidisciplinary care teams, scientific societies, rare-disease networks, and patient organizations while preserving the independence and integrity of scientific exchange&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expert and center mapping:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and segment relevant centers and stakeholders, characterize referral and treatment pathways, and help quantify patient populations and unmet medical needs across France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Medical insights:&lt;/strong&gt; Capture, document, analyze, and communicate actionable field insights to the local and global organization, and close the loop by showing how validated insights inform strategy and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scientific exchange and education:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver balanced, non-promotional scientific exchange; lead advisory boards, expert meetings, congress activities, internal training, and other medical education initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evidence generation:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the local evidence plan, including real-world evidence, registries, epidemiology, outcomes research, collaborative studies, and investigator-sponsored research; support protocol and publication review as appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch and access readiness:&lt;/strong&gt; Support pre-launch and launch activities by clarifying unmet need, patient identification and referral pathways, multidisciplinary care requirements, and evidence gaps; contribute medical input to early or compassionate access activities when applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Medical review:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide robust medical review of scientific, educational, market access, and promotional materials through the appropriate review process, ensuring scientific accuracy, fair balance, and consistency with approved information and company standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Regulatory Affairs, Market Access, Commercial, Patient Advocacy, Pharmacovigilance, Compliance, and global or regional Medical Affairs while maintaining the appropriate separation between medical and promotional activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety and quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and report adverse events, product complaints, and other safety information within required timelines; maintain complete documentation and complete all required training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You&#39;ll Work&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a France-based role with the Paris area as the designated office location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular travel across France is expected, with periodic travel to the International Headquarters in Zug, Switzerland, and to other countries in the Europe West region (Belgium, Netherlands, Eastern Europe)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MD, PharmD, PhD, or another advanced scientific or healthcare degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3-5 years of Medical Affairs experience in the pharmaceutical or biotechnology industry, including meaningful experience in France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to engage healthcare professionals in high-quality scientific exchange and to convert field insights into medical actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing country medical plans, preferably in a launch or pre-launch setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound understanding of the French healthcare system, hospital and expert-center environment, and the compliance framework governing interactions with healthcare stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scientific writing, presentation, and data interpretation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project management skills and the ability to manage several priorities in a small, fast-moving organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and professional English, both written and spoken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Strongly Preferred&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in rare diseases and at least one of the following areas: skeletal dysplasia or pediatrics, neuromuscular disease, endocrinology, or mineral metabolism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with French rare-disease expert centers, networks, scientific societies, or patient organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-world evidence, investigator-sponsored research, publications, or early access programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a biotechnology company or an affiliate being built from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Expected Attributes&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate independently and quickly, with a strong sense of ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scientific curiosity, critical thinking, and methodological rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patient-centered judgment and high ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize across products, stakeholders, and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compelling communication in both French and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directness, clarity, and constructive collaboration in all exchanges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
